div> </div>What do you need it to be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:41:57-07:00","id":1084677,"title":"","content":"Real. So real it hurts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:02:21-07:00","id":1124022,"title":"","content":"bumping this thread so we don't fill up the Hunter/Princess Fan Supplement thread with general Princess discussion. <br /> <br /> Also, question. How do the Twilight Princesses keep up their Sensitivity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:47:02-07:00","id":1124047,"title":"","content":"For Sensitivity:<br /> <br /> Storms can use the Choke it Down to convert a Sensitivity roll into a resistant Lethal damage (resistant means no magical healing).<br /> Mirrors can undo Sensitivity by erasing their memory of it.<br /> Tears don't get any special way to tank Sensitivity and most have low Belief. Instead Tears use their large numbers of Sworn and the infrastructure of Alhambra to take frequent breaks to remove any Shadows. Sending a high Inner Light Princesses against players and letting them use Sensitivity to defeat her (e.g. trick her into seeing the consiquences of her Sworn's actions) is completely appropriate and fitting for the magicial girl &amp; dark magical girl relationship.<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> So for clothing there's a Charm Twenty Faces that gives you civilian clothing. Or you could just handwave it away as a genre convention taking a precidence over realisim, or just say that the Princess has a theme rather than a single outfit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:53:46-07:00","id":1124050,"title":"","content":"Thanks, TKR. I know I could have read the PDF, but I only have so much time in every day.<br /> <br /> About the other one. That's reasonable, but i am still too enamored with the idea of a Dreamlands Transformation Boutique/Monastery where you can buy new outfits that you obtain using magical therapy that helps you express different aspects of yourself to alter your costume<br /> <br /> This could be my first big homebrew!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T17:55:45-07:00","id":1230955,"title":"","content":"I came across an interesting magical girl webcomic Shattered Starlight recently. Here is the about paragraph:<br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Farah Shaughnessy is a magical girl. Or rather, she </span></span></div><i>was</i><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> a magical girl. Now, instead of saving Montreal from the forces of Chaos and Entropy, she\u2019s just trying to hold down a decent job to pay her rent and still trying to get her life together a decade after the breakup of her team. When strange things start happening around her and old enemies start to reappear, Farah has to make a choice: face the things she\u2019s been running from all these years or put down her </span></span></div>astral weapon<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> hockey stick and walk away for good.<br /> <br /> Please read the first 20 or 30 pages and tell me if you think this is something you could use in a chronicle. I personally like the idea of retired magical girls discovering that the veil of ignorance that has protected them for decades has started developing holes.</span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}